    "answer": {
      "short": "$$\\frac{BP}{PC}\\times\\frac{CQ}{QA}\\times\\frac{AR}{RB}=\\frac{11}{4}\\times\\frac{2}{3}\\times\\frac{6}{11}=1.$$\n\nFind the three $x$-intercepts using line equations, then apply the distance formula to obtain the ratios.",
      "worked": "The gradients and point–gradient equations are\n$$\\begin{align*}m_{BC}&=\\frac{11-4}{8-4}=\\frac74\\\\BC:\\quad y-4&=\\frac74(x-4)\\\\m_{CA}&=\\frac{6-4}{2-4}=-1\\\\CA:\\quad y-4&=-(x-4)\\\\m_{AB}&=\\frac{11-6}{8-2}=\\frac56\\\\AB:\\quad y-6&=\\frac56(x-2).\\end{align*}$$\nAt each $x$-intercept, $y=0$:\n$$\\begin{align*}-4&=\\frac74(x_P-4)\\\\x_P&=\\frac{12}{7}\\\\-4&=-(x_Q-4)\\\\x_Q&=8\\\\-6&=\\frac56(x_R-2)\\\\x_R&=-\\frac{26}{5}.\\end{align*}$$\nThus $P=(\\frac{12}{7},0)$, $Q=(8,0)$ and $R=(-\\frac{26}{5},0)$. By the distance formula,\n$$\\begin{align*}BP&=\\sqrt{(8-\\tfrac{12}{7})^2+11^2}=\\frac{11\\sqrt{65}}7\\\\PC&=\\sqrt{(4-\\tfrac{12}{7})^2+4^2}=\\frac{4\\sqrt{65}}7\\\\CQ&=\\sqrt{(8-4)^2+(0-4)^2}=4\\sqrt2\\\\QA&=\\sqrt{(8-2)^2+(0-6)^2}=6\\sqrt2\\\\AR&=\\sqrt{(2+\\tfrac{26}{5})^2+6^2}=\\frac{6\\sqrt{61}}5\\\\RB&=\\sqrt{(8+\\tfrac{26}{5})^2+11^2}=\\frac{11\\sqrt{61}}5.\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{BP}{PC}\\times\\frac{CQ}{QA}\\times\\frac{AR}{RB}&=\\frac{11\\sqrt{65}/7}{4\\sqrt{65}/7}\\times\\frac{4\\sqrt2}{6\\sqrt2}\\times\\frac{6\\sqrt{61}/5}{11\\sqrt{61}/5}\\\\\\frac{BP}{PC}\\times\\frac{CQ}{QA}\\times\\frac{AR}{RB}&=\\frac{11}{4}\\times\\frac23\\times\\frac6{11}\\\\\\frac{BP}{PC}\\times\\frac{CQ}{QA}\\times\\frac{AR}{RB}&=1.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
